WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.741
Claude ported Rockbox

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:02.755
to a nine-dollar

00:00:02.614 --> 00:00:03.828
MP3 player

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.187
The player is

00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:06.661
an unbranded nine-dollar

00:00:06.508 --> 00:00:07.793
MP3 player from

00:00:07.687 --> 00:00:08.595
AliExpress

00:00:08.725 --> 00:00:10.352
with just 512

00:00:10.164 --> 00:00:11.531
kilobytes of memory

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:12.852
and no documentation

00:00:12.991 --> 00:00:14.064
The author paid

00:00:13.875 --> 00:00:15.101
nine dollars and

00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:16.705
seventy-one cents shipped

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:17.996
With the help

00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:18.869
of large language

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.340
models

00:00:19.494 --> 00:00:20.826
Rockbox now runs

00:00:20.638 --> 00:00:21.156
on it

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:22.029
and the author

00:00:21.841 --> 00:00:22.666
says he was

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.810
barely involved

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:25.010
The port produced

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:26.083
a reusable toolkit

00:00:25.895 --> 00:00:27.180
for future ports

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.523
To prove the

00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:29.349
toolkit works

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.858
Claude ported Rockbox

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:31.471
to a second

00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:31.849
player

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.488
the TS47

00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:34.820
in four hours

00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:36.372
Full story on

00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:37.079
the dashboard
